• **#977 (child bash safety checks): already closed, already commented.** The 10:44 comment covers commit `1e5a5e91`. When a parent has a pinned working directory, a sub-agent's bash now refuses git commands that point outside it (--git-dir, --work-tree, -C, GIT_DIR=, GIT_WORK_TREE=), using the parent's exact refusal text, and it runs inside the pinned directory. With that change, every check listed in the issue now applies to the child too: the hard deny list, the confirm rule (refuse, since a child has no user to ask), git redirection, and write detection. The comment also states the limit: this keeps the child in its directory by default but isn't a sandbox, and a bash command using an absolute path can still escape.
